From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: suckbluefrog <suckbluefrog@proton.me>
Date: Fri, 10 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +000
Subject: [PATCH] pool_alloc: type bomb callback

GCC 15 treats an empty function parameter list as a no-argument function.
The alloc pool stores the malloc-failure callback as void (*)(), while
pool_create() receives and pool_alloc() calls a callback with three
arguments.

Use the same typed callback in the struct as the public pool_create()
prototype.

Signed-off-by: suckbluefrog <suckbluefrog@proton.me>
Upstream: not submitted
---
 lib/pool_alloc.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/lib/pool_alloc.c b/lib/pool_alloc.c
index aedbc2c..a9065a5 100644
--- a/lib/pool_alloc.c
+++ b/lib/pool_alloc.c
@@ -9,7 +9,7 @@ struct alloc_pool
 	size_t			size;		/* extent size		*/
 	size_t			quantum;	/* allocation quantum	*/
 	struct pool_extent	*extents;	/* top extent is "live" */
-	void			(*bomb)();	/* called if malloc fails */
+	void			(*bomb)(const char *, const char *, int); /* called if malloc fails */
 	int			flags;
 
 	/* statistical data */
-- 
2.50.0

